# Per-package license exceptions for scripts/check-npm-licenses.sh.
#
# The gate is an ALLOWLIST: only the permissive licenses named in the script
# pass, and anything unrecognized FAILS. This file records the deliberate
# exceptions. It is the npm twin of .license-allowlist, which covers Go.
#
# Format:  <package name>   # why this is acceptable
#
# Rules for adding an entry:
#   - One package per line. Never exempt a whole license family here — if a
#     license should be broadly acceptable, add it to ALLOWED in the script
#     so the decision is visible in one place.
#   - Say WHY, not just what. "MPL-2.0" is not a reason; "build-time only,
#     does not link into the bundle" is.
#   - Prefer REMOVING the dependency to exempting it. An exception is a
#     standing obligation to re-check; an uninstalled package is not.
#
# LGPL IS NOT EXEMPTABLE HERE. We avoid that family outright rather than
# reason case by case about whether a native addon triggers its linking
# obligations. If an LGPL package appears, the answer is to exclude it (see
# the .npmrc in each frontend, which is how sharp's libvips binaries are kept
# off disk), not to add a line to this file.
#
# The scope is PRODUCTION dependencies (`npm ls --omit=dev`), so build tooling
# does not need entries. lightningcss and axe-core are MPL-2.0 and are not
# listed here precisely because they are dev-tree only.
